# Wave W17-T (Route 130): quiet rock — confluence rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a warm mid-grey shore rock where the quiet water begins to gather toward the corridor — driftwood gathers at this confluence in the design (water dressing, nothing built); foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it. Route 130\u2019s own rock — a warm confluence grey: split from Route 129\u2019s shadow-side lee rock by finish (evenly lit vs lee shade) and from Route 131\u2019s ancient blue-grey tower-isle rock by temperature.
